## FENCES, PARTITION, HOLDS
- **Git:** root history writes only `worktree add -b`, ONE commit, ONE `merge --no-ff`. No `worktree remove`, `fetch`, `push`, `stash`, `reset`, `rebase`, `amend`, `prune`, `gc`, `clean`. In the code repo: `gh api -X GET` only; you clone nothing and edit no file there.
- **HTTP:** `gh api -X GET` to the code repo; the Jira site named in the project's `.env` for GETs, the three comment POSTs and the up-to-three transition POSTs (python `-I`, token in-process, never printed). No mailbox, no demo, no hosted or production host, no package or container registry. No az, ssh, docker, npm, tests, build, deploy, mail, chat, Artifact, Docs, PR, merge of any PR, card or `decision_queue.sh`; no message to any human; no comment or edit on any PR.
- **Toolchains:** none are used (no node, no dotnet, no docker); the seat runs python3 and git only.
- **Partition, from this side:** yours are root `main` for the one merge; `.tools/wt-b1688-rec`, `records/b1688`; your Step-0 copy, STATUS, `Briefs/2026-11-18_B1688_evidence/`, `.tools/b1688/`; the Jira writes of the closed list. **Read-only:** the gate folder in Tuesday's `briefs/`, the B1516 STATUS and evidence, `.tools/b1590/scripts/`, `.tools/b1552/scripts/` and `.tools/b1612/` (copy, never edit). **Not yours:** every Jira key but PCOMP-74, PCOMP-80 and PCOMP-81, `2_Project_Files` code, every other seat's tree, open PR #85. **From the other side:** no live seat's kit names the Composer folder or Jira PCOMP (a word scan of the non-`.pre-` SEAT kits of 2026-11-17 and 2026-11-18 for `Security Composer` and `PCOMP` found 0 files; control: this kit names `Security Composer` 9 or more times); the sibling records seat of this wave (NexusAI) writes another project's tree and other Jira keys only.
- **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes: only the closed list, only under the slots; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; no word added to any user-facing text; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP.
- **HOLDS:** no deploy and no statement about the hosted state beyond what C-152 records; no ruling of your own; no label edit or new Task on any issue; no edit of any code or of `DEPLOY.md`; no new lane and no new row; the three tickets are touched only as the closed list says.

